winex11.drv: Copy child client surfaces into top-levels of another depth.

A child window that draws with OpenGL, Vulkan or Direct3D is composited:
each present copies its client window into the top-level's X window.
set_dc_drawable() told neither the DC nor the XRender layer which visual the
drawable has, so both sides counted as the default visual. When the client
window has 24 bits and the top-level the 32-bit ARGB visual, an unscaled copy
went to XCopyArea, the X server answered BadMatch, and the process died.

A top-level drawn by UpdateLayeredWindow() has that visual, in this process
or another; 0008 also gives it to windows with a constant alpha.

A window drawn by UpdateLayeredWindow() shows its bitmap only, so nothing is
copied into it. For the others, read the visual from the X window itself,
give both DCs its depth and format, and let the existing XRender conversion
do the copy. It used to leave the alpha of such a copy at zero, which a
compositor adds to what is behind; it now gets the window's constant alpha.
Without XRender there is no conversion, and the copy is skipped.

A visual that matches no XRender format, as the default one of a 30-bit
screen, kept the format of the last drawable; the default visual now gets
the root window's format.

Free the clip region when the rectangle is empty.

Shown with OpenGL by repro/p10-layered-child: --layer ulw with --target child
and foreign, and with 0008 also --layer constant with them.

Applies to: Valve Wine after GE's preparation (GE-Proton11-12 and 11-14), in order after 0006.
The driver interface version is unchanged (111).

